# End of build

A feature/fix is **not finished** when the code is written. It is finished when
the gate below has been executed (or an item is explicitly waived with a reason).

Everything named in this file is verified to exist. If you find a reference here
that does not resolve, fix this file in the same change — a mandatory rule that
names deleted files teaches every reader to treat the whole thing as advisory,
which destroys the parts that matter.

## Gate (in order)

1. **Typecheck** — `pnpm typecheck` (or package filter) green.
2. **Unit tests** — run the tests you touched / added; green.
3. **Kept smoke** — if the change has a regression risk (canvas camera, chrome
   layering, contrast, deploy-critical UI), a Playwright or scripted probe must
   **exist and pass**, not merely be authored. Writing `e2e/*.spec.ts` without a
   green run ≠ done.
4. **Commit + push** — only when the user asked to ship / finish / PR; then push
   so CI (and Railway) can pick it up.
5. **Live check** — when the job includes deploy or “live”, probe the deployed
   URL (or CI status) for the commit / behaviour. Code on `main` without a live
   check is incomplete if live was in scope.

## Hard rules

- Do **not** say “done”, “shipped”, or “Phase closed” if any in-scope gate step
  failed, hung, or was skipped.
- A hung webServer / e2e / curl is a **blocker**, not a footnote. Retry with
  `reuseExistingServer` (start API/web yourself) or fix the hang, then re-run.
- One-off probe scripts that get deleted are not a substitute for a kept smoke
  when the gap analysis called for CI/e2e.
- A gate you did not watch fire is not a gate. When you add or re-scope one,
  prove it fails on a deliberate negative control, then prove it passes.
- Prefer: fail the gate loudly over a green narrative with missing evidence.

## Running the e2e suite

`pnpm --filter @workstream/web test:e2e`. Let Playwright start its own servers:
`playwright.config.ts` sets `RATE_LIMIT_MAX: 10000` on the API it launches
because e2e creates many projects from one loopback IP. `reuseExistingServer` is
on outside CI, so reusing a plain `pnpm dev` API inherits production throttling
and batches of 4+ spec files fail at project creation. That is the limiter, not
the code.

## Canvas-specific (Workstream)

The canvas is the **Gold Standard 2026 WebGL studio** (Three.js / React Three
Fiber). The SVG `%`-coord studio and its 63 `canvas-*` specs were deleted in the
2026-08-19 prune. Binding doc: `docs/GOLD-STANDARD-2026.md` (supreme), plus
`docs/GOLD-STANDARD-2026-ARCHITECTURE.md` for the scene graph and chrome
layering.

- **Chrome parenting — no DOM chrome inside the R3F `<Canvas>`.** All overlay
  chrome lives in the sibling `[data-testid=webgl-chrome-overlay]` div. Kept
  detector: `e2e/webgl-chrome-detector.spec.ts`, which asserts the canvas
  contains zero `[data-gs-glass-card], [data-camera-chrome]` and that the
  overlay is a sibling, not a descendant.

  Do **not** reach for `CameraChrome` / `camera-chrome-root` /
  `data-camera-chrome` here. That was the SVG studio's portal host, it is
  retired, and `docs/agent-prompts/ui-root-cause-survey.md` §8 explicitly
  forbids introducing it into WebGL: the WebGL dock is plain DOM overlay
  positioning inside the existing `data-webgl-chrome` overlay.

- **Chrome collision:** `e2e/webgl-chrome-collision.spec.ts` collects every
  chrome surface's bounding rect across three states (idle, maximum
  instruments, assets dock open) at two viewports, and asserts they are
  pairwise non-intersecting and on-screen. Run it when you add, move or resize
  any floating card — DOM containment is allowed, geometric overlap is not.

- **Contrast:** `e2e/webgl-contrast-aa.spec.ts` must stay at zero WCAG AA text
  failures across all five modes (survey, sketch, cad, elevation, quote). When
  touching ink tokens or any translucent chrome surface, run it — it flattens
  the composited background, so it catches what eyeballing a token value
  cannot. Two live examples of what eyeballing misses: `--gs-ink-strong` (#111
  paper ink) was being used as the ink on near-black dev-HUD chrome, and a
  `var(--gs-primary, #FBBF24)` fallback kept a pre-pivot amber for a token that
  is now Signal Blue.

- **z-ladder:** the four-tier Canvas-First ladder
  (`--cf-z-canvas|spatial|chrome|app`) is the only source of truth. Raw numeric
  `zIndex`, Tailwind `z-N`, and raw drei `<Html zIndexRange>` pairs are all
  forbidden — use `cfZPair()` from `apps/web/src/components/canvas/cfz.ts`.
  Kept smoke: `e2e/canvas-first-z-stack.spec.ts`. Guarded from two more
  directions on purpose: the `no-restricted-syntax` selectors in
  `eslint.config.mjs` (`Z_TOKEN_SELECTORS`, which the canvas block must
  **spread**, not replace — flat config does not merge same-named rule options)
  and the `inlineZIndex` axis in `scripts/check-css-scales.mjs`. Keep all three.

- **Colour:** `scripts/check-handoff-chrome-colors.mjs` classifies hex in
  `components/canvas/webgl/` per occurrence — a literal in a `style={{}}` /
  `CSSProperties` object or an SVG `stroke=`/`fill=` attribute is chrome and
  must be a token; a Three.js material, light or shader value may stay literal.
  Do not re-add a blanket path exemption; that is what let six chrome hex
  values accumulate behind a "Three.js render values" justification.

- **Ratchet floors:** the reachability, css-scale and colour gates each declare
  a scope floor. They exist because `walk()` returns `[]` for a missing
  directory, which silently turned the reachability gate into a no-op that
  still printed `ok` for three days after the SVG retirement moved its only
  root. Never lower a floor to make CI pass — repoint the root.

## CI

`pnpm run ci` is the authoritative gate and mirrors the GitLab `gate` job.

Pre-commit (husky/lint-staged) covers typecheck, ESLint on the staged files at
`--max-warnings 0`, `vitest related` on the staged set, the nine pure-file-reader
CI ratchets, the source-scraping specs that `related` structurally cannot select,
and a gate script's paired `*.selftest.mjs` when either is staged. It does **not**
run the full suite, `web:check-bundle-size` (a full Next build), or e2e — so a
green hook is still not a green gate. The authoritative
scope list lives in `.husky/pre-commit`; keep it accurate in the same change that
alters the hook.
